## Description

This detection identifies the execution of **Windows PowerShell** on monitored endpoints using **Sysmon Event ID 1 (Process Creation)**.

PowerShell is one of the most powerful administration tools available on Windows systems and is frequently abused by threat actors for execution, persistence, privilege escalation, defense evasion, credential access, and lateral movement.

Monitoring PowerShell execution provides defenders with early visibility into potentially malicious activity while also establishing a baseline of legitimate administrative usage.

