# Analyst Notes

PowerShell remains one of the most commonly abused Windows utilities during cyber attacks. While this detection focuses on identifying PowerShell execution, it serves as the foundation for more advanced detections such as:

- Encoded PowerShell
- PowerShell Download Cradles
- PowerShell Empire
- Invoke-WebRequest abuse
- AMSI bypass attempts
- Living-off-the-Land (LOLBins)

This detection should be used alongside additional behavioral detections to distinguish legitimate administrative activity from malicious PowerShell usage.
